#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:1
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:3
msgid "`nix-hash` - compute the cryptographic hash of a path"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:5
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-hash` \\[`--flat`\\] \\[`--base32`\\] \\[`--truncate`\\] \\[`--type` "
"_hashAlgo_\\] _path…_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:9
msgid ""
"`nix-hash` \\[`--to-base16`\\|`--to-base32`\\|`--to-base64`\\|`--to-sri`\\] "
"\\[`--type` _hashAlgo_\\] _hash…_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:11
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:13
msgid ""
"The command `nix-hash` computes the cryptographic hash of the contents of "
"each _path_ and prints it on standard output. By default, it computes an MD5 "
"hash, but other hash algorithms are available as well. The hash is printed "
"in hexadecimal. To generate the same hash as `nix-prefetch-url` you have to "
"specify multiple arguments, see below for an example."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:20
msgid ""
"The hash is computed over a _serialisation_ of each path: a dump of the file "
"system tree rooted at the path. This allows directories and symlinks to be "
"hashed as well as regular files. The dump is in the _[Nix Archive (NAR)](../"
"store/file-system-object/content-address.md#serial-nix-archive) format_ "
"produced by [`nix-store --dump`](../command-ref/nix-store/dump.md).  Thus, "
"`nix-hash path` yields the same cryptographic hash as `nix-store --dump path "
"| md5sum`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:30
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:32
msgid "`--flat`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:34
msgid ""
"Print the cryptographic hash of the contents of each regular file _path_. "
"That is, instead of computing the hash of the [Nix Archive (NAR)](../store/"
"file-system-object/content-address.md#serial-nix-archive) of _path_, just "
"[directly hash](../store/file-system-object/content-address.md#serial-flat) "
"_path_ as is. This requires _path_ to resolve to a regular file rather than "
"directory. The result is identical to that produced by the GNU commands "
"`md5sum` and `sha1sum`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:42
msgid "`--base16`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:44
msgid "Print the hash in a hexadecimal representation (default)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:46
msgid "`--base32`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:48
msgid ""
"Print the hash in [Nix32](../protocols/nix32.md) representation rather than "
"hexadecimal. This representation is more compact and can be used in Nix "
"expressions (such as in calls to `fetchurl`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:52
msgid "`--base64`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:54
msgid ""
"Similar to `--base32`, but print the hash in a [Base64](https://en.wikipedia."
"org/wiki/Base64) representation, which is more compact than the Nix32 one."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:57
msgid "`--sri`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:59
msgid ""
"Print the hash in [SRI](../glossary.md#gloss-sri) format with Base64 "
"encoding. The type of hash algorithm will be prepended to the hash string, "
"followed by a hyphen (-) and the Base64 hash body."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:63
msgid "`--truncate`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:65
msgid "Truncate hashes longer than 160 bits (such as SHA-256) to 160 bits."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:67
msgid "`--type` _hashAlgo_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:69
msgid ""
"Use the specified cryptographic hash algorithm, which can be one of "
"`blake3`, `md5`, `sha1`, `sha256`, and `sha512`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:72
msgid "`--to-base16`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:74
msgid ""
"Don’t hash anything, but convert the [Nix32](../protocols/nix32.md) hash "
"representation _hash_ to hexadecimal."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:77
msgid "`--to-base32`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:79
msgid ""
"Don’t hash anything, but convert the hexadecimal hash representation _hash_ "
"to [Nix32](../protocols/nix32.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:82
msgid "`--to-base64`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:84
msgid ""
"Don’t hash anything, but convert the hexadecimal hash representation _hash_ "
"to Base64."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:87
msgid "`--to-sri`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:89
msgid ""
"Don’t hash anything, but convert the hexadecimal hash representation _hash_ "
"to SRI."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:92
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:94
msgid "Computing the same hash as `nix-prefetch-url`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:96
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-prefetch-url file://<(echo test)\n"
"1lkgqb6fclns49861dwk9rzb6xnfkxbpws74mxnx01z9qyv1pjpj\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha256 --flat --base32 <(echo test)\n"
"1lkgqb6fclns49861dwk9rzb6xnfkxbpws74mxnx01z9qyv1pjpj\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:103
msgid "Computing hashes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:105
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ mkdir test\n"
"$ echo \"hello\" > test/world\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash test/ (MD5 hash; default)\n"
"8179d3caeff1869b5ba1744e5a245c04\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-store --dump test/ | md5sum (for comparison)\n"
"8179d3caeff1869b5ba1744e5a245c04  -\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha1 test/\n"
"e4fd8ba5f7bbeaea5ace89fe10255536cd60dab6\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha1 --base16 test/\n"
"e4fd8ba5f7bbeaea5ace89fe10255536cd60dab6\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha1 --base32 test/\n"
"nvd61k9nalji1zl9rrdfmsmvyyjqpzg4\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha1 --base64 test/\n"
"5P2Lpfe76upazon+ECVVNs1g2rY=\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha1 --sri test/\n"
"sha1-5P2Lpfe76upazon+ECVVNs1g2rY=\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha256 --flat test/\n"
"error: reading file `test/': Is a directory\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha256 --flat test/world\n"
"5891b5b522d5df086d0ff0b110fbd9d21bb4fc7163af34d08286a2e846f6be03\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

